# Copy to .env and fill in. Every .env file is gitignored; this example is not.

# --- Built into the bundle (public by nature, but still per-environment) ---

# Billing needs no key. Purchases go straight to Google Play Billing from the native
# plugin, which is authorised by the APK's signature and package name rather than by a
# credential — so there is nothing here to configure, and nothing to leak. A browser build
# has no billing at all; see docs/PLAY_UPLOAD.md.

# Sentry DSN. Empty disables crash reporting entirely: the vendor chunk is never
# fetched and nothing is sent. Do not put the production DSN in a debug build —
# a DSN is a write credential for an issue stream.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Firebase Analytics. `on` attaches the provider; anything else keeps it off, so a
# development build, a fork and a debug APK send nothing by default. This flag only says
# whether to ask — `android/app/google-services.json` says which project is reached, and
# without that file Capacitor's Gradle template leaves Firebase out of the build entirely.
# See docs/ANALYTICS.md.
VITE_ANALYTICS=

# Analytics-storage consent at boot, outside regions that ask for consent. `granted` starts
# collection there; anything else starts denied everywhere. In the EEA, the UK and
# Switzerland (as AdMob's UMP reports the region) the switch starts off whatever this says,
# until the player turns it on — see docs/ANALYTICS.md. The privacy policy describes a
# release built with `granted`; change both together.
VITE_ANALYTICS_CONSENT=

# Phones that get Google's test ads even from a release build: the ones you play on
# yourself. Hashed device ids, comma separated; Logcat prints a phone's id the first time
# it requests an ad. Every build but `npm run build:release` serves test ads regardless.
VITE_ADMOB_TEST_DEVICES=

# The feedback form Settings → Help → Feedback opens: an https address, such as the closed
# test's Google Form. Empty sends a mail to the support address instead.
VITE_FEEDBACK_URL=

# --- Release-time only. NEVER prefixed with VITE_, never in the bundle. ---
# Used by `npm run build:release` to upload sourcemaps, which it then deletes from dist/.
# Read from the shell first and from this file second, so either works — the prefix rule
# means Vite loads neither into `process.env`, and reading only the shell made following
# this very file produce "SENTRY_UPLOAD=1 needs SENTRY_ORG, ...". They stay out of the
# bundle regardless: `envPrefix` is VITE_, and nothing here is passed to `define`.
# See docs/DIAGNOSTICS.md.

SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
